From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: ALPC ports within one process

None of the ALPC calls existed. The Windows App SDK's CoreMessagingXP (the dispatcher under WinUI 3) creates its registrar port and connects to it from the same process: App Installer died at NtAlpcCreatePort. Implemented for ports whose server and clients are in one process: named server ports, connection requests and accept with a port context, synchronous requests and their replies (a reply may come with the release flag), datagrams, releases, disconnect notices, the message-attribute helpers, client impersonation (the process's own token). Each port is a handle that is signalled while messages wait on it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in b/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
index d8a20b0..e937d1e 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ x86_64_EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wl,--image-base,0x170000000
 
 SOURCES = \
 	actctx.c \
+	alpc.c \
 	atom.c \
 	crypt.c \
 	debugbuffer.c \
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/alpc.c b/dlls/ntdll/alpc.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e0086d6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/alpc.c
@@ -0,0 +1,631 @@
